 "group": "proofwiki",
 "lines": [
  [
   "P1",
   "Title: Newton-Girard Identities/Proof 1"
  ],
  [
   "P2",
   "Let $X$ be a [[Definition:Set|set]] of $n$ [[Definition:Number|numbers]] $\\set {x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n}$."
  ],
  [
   "P3",
   "Define:"
  ],
  [
   "P4",
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   "P5",
   "{{eqn | l = \\mathbf S_m "
  ],
  [
   "P6",
   "      | r = \\set {\\paren {j_1, \\ldots, j_m} : 1 \\le j_1 < \\cdots < j_m \\le n}"
  ],
  [
   "P7",
   "      | c = $1 \\le m \\le n$"
  ],
  [
   "P8",
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   "P9",
   "{{eqn | l = \\map {e_m} X"
  ],
  [
   "P10",
   "      | r = \\begin {cases} 1 & : m = 0 \\\\ \\ds \\sum_{\\mathbf S_m} x_{j_1} \\cdots x_{j_m} & : 1 \\le m \\le n \\\\ 0 & : m > n \\\\ \\end {cases}"
  ],
  [
   "P11",
   "      | c = {{Defof|Elementary Symmetric Function}}"
  ],
  [
   "P12",
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   "P13",
   "{{eqn | l = \\map {p_k} X"
  ],
  [
   "P14",
   "      | r = \\begin{cases} n & : k = 0 \\\\ \\ds \\sum_{i \\mathop = 1}^n  x_i^k & : k \\ge 1 \\end {cases}"
  ],
  [
   "P15",
   "      | c = {{Defof|Power Sum}}"
  ],
  [
   "P16",
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   "P17",
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   "P18",
   "The '''[[Newton-Girard Identities]]''' are:"
  ],
  [
   "P19",
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   "P20",
   "{{eqn | n = 1"
  ],
  [
   "P21",
   "      | l = k \\map {e_k} X"
  ],
  [
   "P22",
   "      | r = \\sum_{i \\mathop = 1}^k \\paren {-1}^{i - 1} \\map {e_{k - i} } X \\map {p_i} X"
  ],
  [
   "P23",
   "      | c = for $1 \\le k \\le n$"
  ],
  [
   "P24",
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   "P25",
   "{{eqn | n = 2"
  ],
  [
   "P26",
   "      | l = 0"
  ],
  [
   "P27",
   "      | r = \\sum_{i \\mathop = k - n}^k \\paren {-1}^{i - 1} \\map {e_{k - i} } X \\map {p_i} X"
  ],
  [
   "P28",
   "      | c = for $1 \\le n < k$"
  ],
  [
   "P29",
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   "P30",
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   1,
   "=== Outline ==="
  ],
  [
   2,
   ""
  ],
  [
   3,
   "The proof is divided into three cases: $k < n$, $k = n$ and $k > n$."
  ],
  [
   4,
   ""
  ],
  [
   5,
   "The tools are [[Viète's Formulas]], [[Recursion Property of Elementary Symmetric Function]], [[Definition:Telescoping Series|telescoping sums]] and  [[Definition:Homogeneous Function|homogeneous functions]] of degree $k$."
  ],
  [
   6,
   ""
  ],
  [
   7,
   "=== Details ==="
  ],
  [
   8,
   ""
  ],
  [
   9,
   "Discovery of formulas (1)-(2) has humble beginnings:"
  ],
  [
   10,
   ""
  ],
  [
   11,
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   12,
   "{{eqn | n = 3"
  ],
  [
   13,
   "      | l = \\prod_{r \\mathop = 1}^n \\paren { x - x_r } "
  ],
  [
   14,
   "      | r = \\sum_{i \\mathop = 0}^n \\paren {-1}^{n-i} {\\map {e_{n - i} } X} x^i"
  ],
  [
   15,
   "      | c = [[Viète's Formulas]]"
  ],
  [
   16,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   17,
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   18,
   ""
  ],
  [
   19,
   "Create $n$ equations all with {{LHS}} zero by substitution  $x = x_j$ in (3), $1 \\le j \\le n$."
  ],
  [
   20,
   ":$\\ds 0 = \\sum_{i \\mathop = 0}^n \\paren {-1}^{n-i} {\\map {e_{n - i} } X} x_j^i$"
  ],
  [
   21,
   "Then multiply the $j$th equation by $x_j^r$ and add the $n$ equations, for $1 \\le j \\le n$:"
  ],
  [
   22,
   ""
  ],
  [
   23,
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   24,
   "{{eqn | n = 4"
  ],
  [
   25,
   "      | l =  0 "
  ],
  [
   26,
   "      | r = \\sum_{j \\mathop = 1}^n \\sum_{i \\mathop = 0}^n \\paren {-1}^{n - i} \\map {e_{n - i} } X x_j^{i + r}"
  ],
  [
   27,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   28,
   "{{eqn | r = \\sum_{i \\mathop = 0}^n \\paren {-1}^{n - i} \\map {e_{n - i} } X \\map {p_{i + r} } X"
  ],
  [
   29,
   "      | c = Term $\\map {e_m} X$ is zero for $m \\gt n$, affecting case $r \\gt 0$."
  ],
  [
   30,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   31,
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   32,
   ""
  ],
  [
   33,
   "Case $r = 0$ in (4) gives (1) for $k = n$, by isolating term $n \\map {e_n} X$."
  ],
  [
   34,
   ""
  ],
  [
   35,
   "Case $r > 0$ in (4) gives (2) by [[Rules for Manipulating Summations|re-indexing]]: $m = k - n + i$ with $m = k - n$ to $k$."
  ],
  [
   36,
   ""
  ],
  [
   37,
   "<!--"
  ],
  [
   38,
   "Case $k < n$ apparently involves more than this simple idea. Tignol (2001, pp 38-39) documents the difficulties and provides a complete proof of (1)-(2) using multinomial identities, claiming that his proof \"is perhaps not very different from Newton’s own calculations.\""
  ],
  [
   39,
   "-->"
  ],
  [
   40,
   ""
  ],
  [
   41,
   "Case $k < n$ in (1), not yet discussed, does not use multiply and add as in (4)."
  ],
  [
   42,
   ""
  ],
  [
   43,
   "The key ingredient:"
  ],
  [
   44,
   ""
  ],
  [
   45,
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   46,
   "{{eqn | n = 5"
  ],
  [
   47,
   "      | l = \\map {e_m} {z_1, \\ldots, z_p, z_{p + 1} }"
  ],
  [
   48,
   "      | r = z_{p + 1} \\map {e_{m - 1} } {z_1, \\ldots, z_p} + \\map {e_m} {z_1, \\ldots, z_p}"
  ],
  [
   49,
   "      | c = [[Recursion Property of Elementary Symmetric Function]], valid for $1 \\le m \\le p$."
  ],
  [
   50,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   51,
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   52,
   ""
  ],
  [
   53,
   "The {{RHS}} of (1) is:"
  ],
  [
   54,
   ""
  ],
  [
   55,
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   56,
   "{{eqn | n = 6"
  ],
  [
   57,
   "      | r =  \\sum_{i \\mathop = 1}^k \\paren {-1}^{i - 1} \\sum_{j \\mathop = 1}^n \\map {e_{k - i} } X x_j^i"
  ],
  [
   58,
   "      | o ="
  ],
  [
   59,
   "      | c = Replace in (1) each [[Definition:Power Sum|power sum]] $p_i$ by its summation."
  ],
  [
   60,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   61,
   "{{eqn | ll = \\leadsto"
  ],
  [
   62,
   "      | r =  \\paren {-1}^{k - 1} \\sum_{m \\mathop = 0}^{k - 1} \\paren {-1}^m \\sum_{j \\mathop = 1}^n \\map {e_m} X x_j^{k - m}"
  ],
  [
   63,
   "      | o ="
  ],
  [
   64,
   "      | c = [[Rules for Manipulating Summations|Re-index]] with $m = k - i$ and adjust powers of $-1$."
  ],
  [
   65,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   66,
   "{{eqn | ll = \\leadsto"
  ],
  [
   67,
   "      | r =  \\paren {-1}^{k - 1} \\sum_{j \\mathop = 1}^n \\paren {\\map {e_0} X x_j^k + \\sum_{m \\mathop = 1}^{k - 1} \\paren {-1}^m \\paren {x_j \\map {e_{m - 1} } {U_j} x_j^{k - m} + \\map {e_m} {U_j} x_j^{k - m} } }"
  ],
  [
   68,
   "      | o ="
  ],
  [
   69,
   "      | c = by (5), where $U_j = X \\setminus \\set {x_j}$"
  ],
  [
   70,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   71,
   "{{eqn | ll= \\leadsto"
  ],
  [
   72,
   "      | r =  \\paren {-1}^{k - 1} \\sum_{j \\mathop = 1}^n \\paren {\\map {e_0} X x_j^k + \\sum_{m \\mathop = 1}^{k - 1} \\paren {-1}^m \\map {e_{m - 1} } {U_j} x_j^{k - m + 1} + \\sum_{m \\mathop = 1}^{k - 1} \\paren {-1}^m \\map {e_m} {U_j} {x_j^{k - m} } }"
  ],
  [
   73,
   "      | o ="
  ],
  [
   74,
   "      | c = [[Rules for Manipulating Summations|adjust summations]] and collect powers of $x_j$"
  ],
  [
   75,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   76,
   "{{eqn | ll = \\leadsto"
  ],
  [
   77,
   "      | n = 7"
  ],
  [
   78,
   "      | r =  \\paren {-1}^{k - 1} \\sum_{j \\mathop = 1}^n \\paren {-1}^{k - 1} x_j \\map {e_k} {U_j}"
  ],
  [
   79,
   "      | o ="
  ],
  [
   80,
   "      | c = [[Definition:Telescoping Series|telescoping sum]] reduces to a single term"
  ],
  [
   81,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   82,
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   83,
   ""
  ],
  [
   84,
   "It remains to prove (7) matches (1):"
  ],
  [
   85,
   ""
  ],
  [
   86,
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   87,
   "{{eqn | n = 8"
  ],
  [
   88,
   "      | l = \\sum_{j \\mathop = 1}^n x_j \\map {e_k} {X \\setminus \\set {x_j} }"
  ],
  [
   89,
   "      | r = k \\map {e_k} X"
  ],
  [
   90,
   "      | c = for $1 \\le k \\le n$"
  ],
  [
   91,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   92,
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   93,
   ""
  ],
  [
   94,
   "Define:"
  ],
  [
   95,
   ""
  ],
  [
   96,
   ":$\\map {y_i} t = t\\, x_i, 1 \\le i \\le n$"
  ],
  [
   97,
   ""
  ],
  [
   98,
   ":$X_t = \\set {\\map {y_1} t, \\ldots, \\map {y_n} t}$"
  ],
  [
   99,
   ""
  ],
  [
   100,
   ":$\\map f t = \\map {e_k} {tx_1, \\ldots, tx_n}$."
  ],
  [
   101,
   ""
  ],
  [
   102,
   "Then there are two equations (9)-(10) for $\\map {f'} t$:"
  ],
  [
   103,
   ""
  ],
  [
   104,
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   105,
   "{{eqn | n = 9"
  ],
  [
   106,
   "      | l = \\map {f'} t "
  ],
  [
   107,
   "      | r = \\sum_{j \\mathop = 1}^n x_j \\map {e_k} {X_t \\setminus \\set {\\map {y_j} t} }"
  ],
  [
   108,
   "      | c = [[Chain Rule for Real-Valued Functions|chain rule]] for several variables"
  ],
  [
   109,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   110,
   "{{eqn | n = 10"
  ],
  [
   111,
   "      | l = \\map f t "
  ],
  [
   112,
   "      | r = t^k \\map {e_k} X"
  ],
  [
   113,
   "      | c = because $f$ is a [[Definition:Homogeneous Function|homogeneous function]] of degree $k$"
  ],
  [
   114,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   115,
   "{{eqn | ll= \\leadsto"
  ],
  [
   116,
   "      | l = \\map {f'} t"
  ],
  [
   117,
   "      | r = k t^{k - 1} \\map {e_k} X"
  ],
  [
   118,
   "      | c = [[Power Rule for Derivatives]]"
  ],
  [
   119,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   120,
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   121,
   ""
  ],
  [
   122,
   "Let $t = 1$ in (9) and (10) to prove (8)."
  ],
  [
   123,
   "{{qed}}"
  ],
  [
   124,
   ""
  ],
  [
   125,
   "[[Category:Newton-Girard Identities]]"
  ]
 ],
